\"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"def263c5651e6c7a14e0eae65a4d4dddd24d4dea9229424fb959badb540f48a3","event_uuid":"9c832759-c0f3-4470-b8e9-3ed7d5744049","position":{"commit_sha":"1c5989565a5de17284f79b43114e47bf06841bac","position":"1794260978800308001-9c832759-c0f3-4470-b8e9-3ed7d5744049"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794255966080541001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"21b6bc96-fee2-4dea-aca3-1a3814033c92","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0376-8839-dc75-4260"},{"link_uuid":"107c5321-27fc-4141-8f53-c80eedeb1d2d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"b690-7231-22fe-49e4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe epic's last acceptance criterion is a production check: after deploy, one `review-plan` per engine completes on a live ticket through the production MCP server, with the verdict, engine and attestation recorded. Unit tests cannot show that the deployed server, its signing environment and its Bedrock credentials work with the new engine and models.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the engine children have landed and the production MCP server is deployed at a commit containing them (confirmed from the server's reported version), pick one open, claimable ticket and run `review_plan_start` twice through the production MCP server, once with `engine=\"pipeline\"` and once with `engine=\"agentic\"`, polling `gate_status` and `plan_review_status` to completion. Record for each run, in a comment on the epic: the job id, verdict, engine, model, attestation presence (and that `review-plan --status` reports it current), and the run's completion timestamp in PST. No production configuration is changed; both runs use the explicit per-call argument. Using the MCP async surface is the production path agents actually use, so it is the right one to prove.\n\n## Scope\n\nNone. This is an operational verification: no repository file changes. Evidence lives in a comment on the epic `pompous-vitriolic-macaw`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [non-codebase] One production `review_plan_start` run per engine completes on a live ticket; the job ids, verdicts, engines, models, attestation status and PST completion timestamps are recorded in a comment on the epic.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","0376-8839-dc75-4260"],["depends_on","b690-7231-22fe-49e4"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change: operational verification against the deployed production MCP server. Where output or evidence lives: a comment on epic pompous-vitriolic-macaw with job ids, verdicts, engines, models and attestation status.","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"526b-ae76-a409-4aaf","ticket_type":"task","title":"Production verification: one review-plan per engine on the live MCP server","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["06a400e9-344b-4520-9e3c-8757133f24f3","21b6bc96-fee2-4dea-aca3-1a3814033c92","107c5321-27fc-4141-8f53-c80eedeb1d2d","9c832759-c0f3-4470-b8e9-3ed7d5744049"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794260978800308002,"uuid":"55f79ce8-f60b-43fc-b1d5-5cd75e909dfb"}